<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05GG">Lemma <span data-tag="05GG">10.1.3.13</span>.</a> Let $k \geq 0$ and $n$ be integers, let $K = \{  1, \cdots , k \} $, and let $P^{\leq n}(K)$ denote the partially ordered collection of all subsets $J \subseteq K$ which have cardinality $\leq n$. Then the assignment $J \mapsto \alpha _{J}$ of Construction <a data-tag="05GD" href="/tag/05GD">10.1.3.10</a> determines a right cofinal functor of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \alpha : \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( P^{\leq n}(K) ) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{ [k] / }^{\leq n})^{\operatorname{op}}. \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Corollary <a data-tag="02P3" href="/tag/02P3">7.2.3.7</a>, since the functor $\alpha $ has a left adjoint (which carries a morphism $f: [k] \rightarrow [m]$ to the subset $J = \{  j \in K: f(j-1) &lt; f(j) \}  \in P^{\leq n}(K)$). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
